{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 10, 13]], "date-time": "2026-10-13T15:24:50Z", "timestamp": 1791905090162, "version": "4.3.4"}, "reference-count": 15, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "S1", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2019, 6, 12]], "date-time": "2019-06-12T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1560297600000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 11, "URL": "http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/termsAndConditions#vor"}], "content-domain": {"domain": ["onlinelibrary.wiley.com"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "short-container-title": ["Hematological Oncology"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2019, 6]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title><jats:p>Chimeric antigen receptor (CAR) T\u2010cell therapy has the potential to revolutionize the management of B\u2010cell lymphomas and possibly other cancers. Two anti\u2010CD19 CAR T\u2010cell products, axicabtagene ciloleucel and tisagenlecleucel, have been approved for the management of relapsed/refractory large B\u2010cell lymphoma after two lines of systemic therapy. Additional trials are ongoing to evaluate these and other CAR T products at earlier stages of the disease course as well as in other lymphomas. While the potential to induce durable remissions with a single CAR T\u2010cell infusion even in patients who are chemorefractory has generated much enthusiasm in the field, practitioners need to familiarize themselves with the unique toxicities associated with these therapies. This review will discuss the grading and management of the two most common toxicities, cytokine release syndrome (CRS) and immune effector cell\u2010associated neurotoxicity syndrome (ICANS), observed acutely after this therapy. In addition, late toxicities including prolonged cytopenias and on\u2010target off\u2010tumor effects will be reviewed.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1002/hon.2595", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2019, 6, 12]], "date-time": "2019-06-12T08:00:51Z", "timestamp": 1560326451000}, "page": "48-52", "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.1002/crossmark_policy", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 282, "title": ["Managing the toxicities of CAR T\u2010cell therapy"], "prefix": "10.1002", "volume": "37", "author": [{"given": "Sattva S.", "family": "Neelapu", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Department of Lymphoma and Myeloma, Division of Cancer Medicine The University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center  Houston Texas"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "311", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2019, 6, 12]]}, "reference": [{"key": "e_1_2_9_2_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1056/NEJMoa1707447"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_3_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1056/NEJMoa1804980"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_4_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1200/JCO.2018.36.15_suppl.7505"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_5_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/nrclinonc.2017.128"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_6_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/nrclinonc.2017.148"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_7_1", "article-title": "ASBMT consensus grading for cytokine release syndrome and neurologic toxicity associated with immune effector cells", "author": "Lee DW", "year": "2018", "journal-title": "Biol Blood Marrow Transplant"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_8_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1182/blood-2014-05-552729"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_9_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1056/NEJMoa1407222"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_10_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1182/blood-2017-06-793141"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_11_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1158/2159-8290.CD-17-0698"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_12_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/s41591-018-0036-4"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_13_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/s41591-018-0041-7"}, {"key": "e_1_2_9_14_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "